1
00:00:05,514 --> 00:00:07,280
How could you do this?

2
00:00:07,315 --> 00:00:09,680
But was this the real reason you went back to him?

3
00:00:10,438 --> 00:00:13,840
As long as I'm alive, you'll never get what you want.

4
00:00:14,102 --> 00:00:17,640
In the end was the path I chose truly worth it?

5
00:00:19,350 --> 00:00:21,080
Tinnakorn asked me to give you this.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:26,320
Please, don't leave me. Please?

7
00:00:26,672 --> 00:00:28,680
We are two people who can't be in love.

8
00:00:29,320 --> 00:00:30,321
Let me go.

9
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:32,468
I wish you all the best.

10
00:02:18,967 --> 00:02:19,968
I love you.

11
00:02:23,064 --> 00:02:24,242
I love you, too.

12
00:02:25,933 --> 00:02:28,122
Even if I have to wait months, years,

13
00:02:28,616 --> 00:02:29,617
or the rest of my life,

14
00:02:30,413 --> 00:02:32,562
you’re the only one I’ll ever wait for.

15
00:02:33,949 --> 00:02:37,266
No matter what happens, I will forever be…

16
00:02:38,386 --> 00:02:39,387
your Phobthee.

17
00:02:43,882 --> 00:02:44,883
Tin, darling.

18
00:02:51,608 --> 00:02:52,609
Grandma.

19
00:02:53,869 --> 00:02:54,870
Grandma.

20
00:02:56,557 --> 00:02:57,558
Grandma.

21
00:03:03,325 --> 00:03:05,162
I went to see Phob.

22
00:03:06,520 --> 00:03:08,042
What did he say?

23
00:03:11,304 --> 00:03:13,842
He told me he wanted us to go back to the way we were.

24
00:03:16,252 --> 00:03:17,253
To be the same?

25
00:03:17,746 --> 00:03:19,784
How could we go back to the way we were?

26
00:03:21,304 --> 00:03:22,642
How could we do that?

27
00:03:30,824 --> 00:03:31,925
You poor thing.

28
00:03:37,101 --> 00:03:40,052
I used to think the greatest obstacle between Phop and me

29
00:03:40,533 --> 00:03:43,194
was that we were different from everyone else,

30
00:03:43,962 --> 00:03:46,405
that society would never accept us.

31
00:03:47,082 --> 00:03:49,602
But I believed that as long as we loved each other enough,

32
00:03:49,652 --> 00:03:51,653
we could face it together and make it through.

33
00:03:52,122 --> 00:03:54,802
But today, I realized that the problem was never anyone else.

34
00:03:54,823 --> 00:03:56,082
It was me.

35
00:03:56,490 --> 00:03:58,802
I’m the one he wants to change, Grandma.

36
00:03:58,891 --> 00:04:00,442
I'm part of the system he wants…

37
00:04:01,114 --> 00:04:03,162
he wants to dismantle.

38
00:04:04,341 --> 00:04:06,602
How can we be together?

39
00:04:06,642 --> 00:04:08,458
How can we be in love after this?

40
00:04:13,109 --> 00:04:14,842
It's okay, darling.

41
00:04:16,357 --> 00:04:17,840
You still have me.

42
00:04:18,237 --> 00:04:19,538
I'm right here with you.

43
00:04:22,189 --> 00:04:23,482
It's going to be okay, darling.

44
00:04:34,854 --> 00:04:35,855
Sakchai.

45
00:04:37,909 --> 00:04:38,910
Sakchai, hi.

46
00:04:40,002 --> 00:04:41,003
Where are you heading to?

47
00:04:42,386 --> 00:04:43,402
To the mine?

48
00:04:44,056 --> 00:04:45,402
Good, I'll go with you.

49
00:04:45,702 --> 00:04:48,362
Oh, come on! There is no mining business.

50
00:04:55,562 --> 00:04:57,493
Then how...

51
00:04:58,298 --> 00:04:59,299
how did we make a profit before?

52
00:05:00,346 --> 00:05:01,347
That money...

53
00:05:01,600 --> 00:05:03,954
was just bait to sucker more idiots into investing.

54
00:05:09,117 --> 00:05:10,242
You fooled me?

55
00:05:13,389 --> 00:05:14,642
Are you lying to me?

56
00:05:16,018 --> 00:05:18,202
You son of a bitch!

57
00:05:18,354 --> 00:05:19,482
You fooled me?

58
00:05:19,834 --> 00:05:22,242
You lied to me! Do you even know who I am, huh?

59
00:05:22,517 --> 00:05:23,562
How dare you lie to me?

60
00:05:36,472 --> 00:05:38,522
Do you know who you are now?

61
00:05:40,045 --> 00:05:42,282
Do you still think being part of the royal family

62
00:05:42,613 --> 00:05:43,702
means anything anymore?

63
00:05:44,578 --> 00:05:48,202
If you still had any power, you wouldn't be this desperate for money.

64
00:05:53,074 --> 00:05:55,720
That’s the ministry’s money! It’s ministry money!

65
00:05:56,029 --> 00:05:57,702
Give me my money back.

66
00:05:58,056 --> 00:06:01,802
I’ll go to jail if I don’t have that money! I have to pay it back!

67
00:06:02,157 --> 00:06:03,158
It's none of my business.

68
00:06:03,469 --> 00:06:06,122
You're stupid enough to steal the money!

69
00:06:06,702 --> 00:06:07,703
Go!

70
00:06:08,562 --> 00:06:10,402
Hey!

71
00:06:10,474 --> 00:06:11,762
Don't go! Give me the money!

72
00:06:12,442 --> 00:06:14,762
Give me the money, Sakchai!

73
00:06:20,368 --> 00:06:22,562
I don't want to go to jail!

74
00:06:34,461 --> 00:06:37,133
Chat, darling. Wait.

75
00:06:37,357 --> 00:06:39,962
- What happened to you? Why did you look like this?
- Grandma.

76
00:06:39,992 --> 00:06:41,682
I'm so exhausted, I need to rest.

77
00:06:41,722 --> 00:06:43,642
Tell me what is going on?

78
00:06:43,773 --> 00:06:46,402
M.C. Chatthorn Varakulvatin,

79
00:06:47,101 --> 00:06:49,802
You have been charged with embezzling funds

80
00:06:50,076 --> 00:06:51,842
from the Ministry of Finance.

81
00:06:55,189 --> 00:06:56,522
What kind of ridiculous charge is that?

82
00:06:57,658 --> 00:06:59,202
My son is not an embezzler.

83
00:06:59,568 --> 00:07:01,181
The People's Committee of Siam audited the accounts

84
00:07:01,293 --> 00:07:04,322
audited the accounts Prince Chatthorn was responsible for

85
00:07:04,466 --> 00:07:06,762
and found that as much as 200,000 baht was missing.

86
00:07:10,434 --> 00:07:12,482
Phob is trying to attack on us.

87
00:07:13,106 --> 00:07:14,607
He is framing my son.

88
00:07:15,613 --> 00:07:17,922
He has been fired, how could he embezzle from the ministry?

89
00:07:19,722 --> 00:07:21,302
And we're talking about 200,000 baht.

90
00:07:22,037 --> 00:07:24,042
If you're saying Chat really took the money, do you have any proof?

91
00:07:24,106 --> 00:07:25,802
All the evidence is at the police station.

92
00:07:26,069 --> 00:07:28,922
I suggest you cooperate and come with me.

93
00:07:29,149 --> 00:07:30,370
Officer, take him.

94
00:07:30,525 --> 00:07:31,526
No!

95
00:07:31,965 --> 00:07:33,082
Dad! Grandma!

96
00:07:33,250 --> 00:07:36,122
Dad! Don't let them do this to me! Dad!

97
00:07:36,264 --> 00:07:37,482
Dad! Help me!

98
00:07:38,405 --> 00:07:40,482
Oh my! Your Highness!

99
00:07:52,354 --> 00:07:53,355
Phob, I have bad news.

100
00:07:53,562 --> 00:07:56,002
Prince Chatthorn has been arrested for embezzling funds from the ministry.

101
00:08:49,949 --> 00:08:52,498
Dad! Dad!

102
00:08:54,248 --> 00:08:55,702
Please help me!

103
00:09:02,918 --> 00:09:06,502
How could you be such a fool and fall for that mining scheme?

104
00:09:08,076 --> 00:09:10,762
And you even used ministry funds to invest in it?

105
00:09:11,624 --> 00:09:13,362
That was public money, you idiot!

106
00:09:15,128 --> 00:09:16,129
I'm sorry.

107
00:09:17,042 --> 00:09:19,302
It's my fault, I was so stupid.

108
00:09:20,117 --> 00:09:22,482
Please help me, I can't be in here.

109
00:09:22,522 --> 00:09:24,402
I couldn't sleep last night, there were so many mosquitoes.

110
00:09:24,442 --> 00:09:25,762
Now you're crying.

111
00:09:26,549 --> 00:09:27,922
Why didn't you think before you act?

112
00:09:28,506 --> 00:09:31,302
The Khana Ratsadon has been looking for any excuse to go after the royals.

113
00:09:31,944 --> 00:09:35,402
And now the People's Committee has more power than anyone.

114
00:09:36,146 --> 00:09:38,642
Not a single minister or director-general

115
00:09:38,664 --> 00:09:40,562
would dare step in to help.

116
00:09:44,450 --> 00:09:45,451
I…

117
00:09:46,492 --> 00:09:48,642
I looked into the documents that the police showed.

118
00:09:50,393 --> 00:09:54,762
You're the only person authorized to handle pension payments
for the Department of Mineral Resources.

119
00:09:56,730 --> 00:09:59,402
If this goes to court,

120
00:10:03,642 --> 00:10:04,643
I…

121
00:10:05,461 --> 00:10:07,602
I think you will go to jail for many years.

122
00:10:08,394 --> 00:10:10,898
I can't go to jail, Tin. I really can't.

123
00:10:10,912 --> 00:10:13,288
I can't go to jail. You need to help me!

124
00:10:13,362 --> 00:10:16,322
Tin…you need to help me! I really can't go to jail.

125
00:10:16,690 --> 00:10:18,042
Dad…please help me.

126
00:10:18,226 --> 00:10:21,082
- I can't go to jail--
- Shut up!

127
00:10:23,653 --> 00:10:27,002
You're crying and wailing like that, aren’t you ashamed?

128
00:10:30,010 --> 00:10:33,602
Have some dignity. Act like a child of mine.

129
00:10:49,741 --> 00:10:50,742
Tin.

130
00:10:51,029 --> 00:10:52,336
- Chat.
- Tin, don't leave me here.

131
00:10:52,739 --> 00:10:55,042
Look at them! Didn't you see them?

132
00:10:55,717 --> 00:10:58,282
- Chat.
- Look at them!

133
00:10:59,882 --> 00:11:00,883
I will try to help you out of here.

134
00:11:04,397 --> 00:11:05,602
Don't leve me here, please.

135
00:11:07,202 --> 00:11:08,842
Tin, don't leave me here.

136
00:11:09,544 --> 00:11:11,922
Look at them! Tin! Don't leave me.

137
00:11:19,410 --> 00:11:22,642
Damrong, you know someone on the People's Committee, don't you?

138
00:11:23,752 --> 00:11:26,242
Could you use your connections to help my son?

139
00:11:29,829 --> 00:11:32,002
You've known Chatthorn since he was a boy, Damrong.

140
00:11:32,773 --> 00:11:34,122
He's like one of your own.

141
00:11:35,354 --> 00:11:38,042
And soon enough, we'll be family through marriage.

142
00:11:38,885 --> 00:11:40,642
I can't help you with Chatthorn.

143
00:11:43,381 --> 00:11:47,402
About Tinnakorn and Ruethaisiri's engagement,

144
00:11:48,882 --> 00:11:50,122
we should call it off for now.

145
00:11:52,312 --> 00:11:54,002
Why do you suddenly want to call off the engagement?

146
00:11:55,302 --> 00:11:56,722
The country is in turmoil.

147
00:11:57,600 --> 00:12:00,601
Besides, it's not as though they'll be getting married anytime soon.

148
00:12:01,104 --> 00:12:02,205
We might as well call off the engagement for now.

149
00:12:05,578 --> 00:12:06,579
Uncle?

150
00:12:07,376 --> 00:12:10,122
Uncle, could you…

151
00:12:10,789 --> 00:12:12,202
- help my brother--
- Enough, Tin.

152
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:17,042
Don't use the state of the country as an excuse.

153
00:12:17,962 --> 00:12:19,282
Don't think I don't know that

154
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:22,002
you've been cozying up to the Khana Ratsadon,

155
00:12:22,234 --> 00:12:24,098
hoping to use your connections to further your business interests.

156
00:12:24,488 --> 00:12:27,162
Is that why you want nothing more to do with the Varakulvatin family?

157
00:12:29,384 --> 00:12:32,482
You're royalty, for God's sake, yet you bow and scrape before commoners.

158
00:12:32,845 --> 00:12:34,042
Have you no dignity?

159
00:12:34,522 --> 00:12:36,242
Isn't it precisely because I've been 'bowing to commoners'

160
00:12:36,384 --> 00:12:38,882
and have connections in the the Khana Ratsadon

161
00:12:39,056 --> 00:12:40,482
that you came begging me to help?

162
00:12:41,781 --> 00:12:43,602
Your own son disgraced himself

163
00:12:43,973 --> 00:12:46,562
by stealing public money, and you still have the nerve to criticize me?

164
00:12:47,834 --> 00:12:49,682
If you're so capable, then find a way to help him yourselves.

165
00:12:50,169 --> 00:12:52,362
I'm staying out of this. I won't let your mess drag me down with you.

166
00:13:08,994 --> 00:13:12,440
Why do you have to cut ties with them like that?

167
00:13:13,096 --> 00:13:14,202
Isn't this what you wanted?

168
00:13:14,664 --> 00:13:16,762
You wanted to break off your engagement to Tinnakorn anyway.

169
00:13:18,085 --> 00:13:19,882
I don't want to marry him

170
00:13:20,245 --> 00:13:22,283
because I don't want to force him into a marriage he doesn't want.

171
00:13:23,034 --> 00:13:24,589
But that doesn't mean I want to cut ties with him completely,

172
00:13:24,829 --> 00:13:28,362
especially now, when he's already down and needs our help the most.

173
00:13:28,917 --> 00:13:30,122
You need to listen to me.

174
00:13:30,650 --> 00:13:34,242
Vasin is a is a Blue Mark. He's on the opposite side from them.

175
00:13:34,554 --> 00:13:37,602
If we get involved with him, we'll only end up getting into trouble ourselves.

176
00:13:37,658 --> 00:13:40,682
You used to condemn the Khana Ratsadon

177
00:13:41,402 --> 00:13:44,722
as traitors to the country.

178
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:49,724
So why are you taking their side now?

179
00:13:51,442 --> 00:13:54,002
Or is it simply about money

180
00:13:54,778 --> 00:13:56,242
and what you stand to gain?

181
00:13:56,533 --> 00:13:58,842
Yes, it is.

182
00:13:59,058 --> 00:14:00,922
It's about our interests and our survival.

183
00:14:01,344 --> 00:14:03,442
You're a woman. What could you possibly understand about any of this?

184
00:14:03,861 --> 00:14:05,682
Now shut your mouth and do as I say.

185
00:14:06,586 --> 00:14:10,322
From now on, stay away from Tinnakorn and Varakulvatin family.

186
00:14:20,813 --> 00:14:22,602
No matter who we turn to for help,

187
00:14:22,614 --> 00:14:24,202
no one is willing to help us, Grandma.

188
00:14:24,704 --> 00:14:29,562
Even the royals who oppose the Khana Ratsadon don't dare step in to help us.

189
00:14:30,178 --> 00:14:31,442
They're afraid they'll get into trouble too.

190
00:14:32,328 --> 00:14:36,442
Does that mean there's really nothing we can do to help Chat?

191
00:14:36,690 --> 00:14:38,722
Your Highness!

192
00:14:38,973 --> 00:14:39,975
What is going on?

193
00:14:40,744 --> 00:14:41,745
He's here.

194
00:14:42,589 --> 00:14:44,502
- He's here.
- Who's here?

195
00:14:51,234 --> 00:14:52,362
Chatthorn?

196
00:14:53,042 --> 00:14:54,482
- Chatthorn?
- Grandma.

197
00:14:54,802 --> 00:14:55,803
Darling?

198
00:14:56,122 --> 00:14:57,402
You know what?

199
00:14:57,576 --> 00:15:00,602
I couldn't sleep last night. Look at the mosquito bites.

200
00:15:00,760 --> 00:15:02,042
How did you get here?

201
00:15:02,413 --> 00:15:05,642
That's right. Why were you released from jail?

202
00:15:05,904 --> 00:15:06,905
Right.

203
00:15:13,898 --> 00:15:16,202
I've been appointed as counsel

204
00:15:16,525 --> 00:15:18,282
to handle this case.

205
00:15:19,240 --> 00:15:22,722
The People's Committee is concerned that if he was sentenced outright,

206
00:15:22,957 --> 00:15:24,802
it might be seen as persecution.

207
00:15:25,410 --> 00:15:27,302
So they've decided to make an exception

208
00:15:27,400 --> 00:15:29,562
and give him chance to prove his innocence.

209
00:15:30,125 --> 00:15:31,242
An exception?

210
00:15:31,522 --> 00:15:34,923
So he is not going to jail anymore?

211
00:15:35,373 --> 00:15:37,122
I am not going to jail.

212
00:15:37,602 --> 00:15:39,802
If we can find 200,000 baht

213
00:15:40,136 --> 00:15:42,082
to return to the ministry within two weeks.

214
00:15:43,896 --> 00:15:45,842
They gave you only two weeks?

215
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:49,610
Yes, Your Highness. They're already being very lenient in this case.

216
00:15:50,117 --> 00:15:51,702
Fortunately, someone spoke up for him,

217
00:15:52,736 --> 00:15:55,703
so he was given a chance to make things right.

218
00:15:56,786 --> 00:15:59,242
Who spoke up for him?

219
00:16:02,120 --> 00:16:03,922
I'm sorry but I really can't say.

220
00:16:05,922 --> 00:16:07,202
Will you excuse me?

221
00:16:11,730 --> 00:16:12,882
Grandma,

222
00:16:13,378 --> 00:16:15,922
I miss you the most.

223
00:16:15,979 --> 00:16:18,402
I will sleep so well tonight.

224
00:16:35,701 --> 00:16:36,702
Your Highness?

225
00:16:41,890 --> 00:16:43,722
You're the one who helped Chat, aren't you?

226
00:16:48,002 --> 00:16:49,003
That's right.

227
00:16:51,186 --> 00:16:52,722
It was me who helped him out.

228
00:16:54,498 --> 00:16:56,162
But you can trust me.

229
00:16:57,533 --> 00:16:58,802
I don't have any hidden agenda.

230
00:16:59,534 --> 00:17:00,535
I didn't say anything.

231
00:17:02,648 --> 00:17:03,902
I'm here to thank you.

232
00:17:06,173 --> 00:17:09,242
By reaching out to help us when our family has fallen on hard times,

233
00:17:10,458 --> 00:17:12,402
you may be putting yourself at risk as well.

234
00:17:14,341 --> 00:17:16,242
I'm truly grateful. More than I can say.

235
00:17:18,192 --> 00:17:20,082
Please don't be sarcastic with me.

236
00:17:21,165 --> 00:17:22,202
I'm not being sarcastic.

237
00:17:24,362 --> 00:17:25,363
It's true.

238
00:17:27,672 --> 00:17:30,044
We don't have any power anymore.

239
00:17:31,448 --> 00:17:35,102
My dad is standing on the different side of yours.

240
00:17:36,589 --> 00:17:38,082
If you stay involved with me,

241
00:17:38,969 --> 00:17:40,242
you'll only be putting yourself at risk.

242
00:18:10,570 --> 00:18:11,802
But I'm willing to take that risk.

243
00:18:14,277 --> 00:18:15,282
All I ask is that

244
00:18:17,088 --> 00:18:19,042
we go back to the way we were.

245
00:18:22,686 --> 00:18:23,687
Can we?

246
00:18:26,677 --> 00:18:28,322
Will you forgive me?

247
00:18:34,637 --> 00:18:36,402
There's nothing for me to forgive.

248
00:18:38,144 --> 00:18:39,402
You have your reasons,

249
00:18:40,826 --> 00:18:42,002
your beliefs,

250
00:18:44,133 --> 00:18:46,002
and the things you believe you have to do.

251
00:18:51,912 --> 00:18:54,922
We're no longer just two people who love each other.

252
00:18:58,978 --> 00:19:00,682
You belong to the new system,

253
00:19:01,544 --> 00:19:03,162
while I am from Varakulvatin family.

254
00:19:04,450 --> 00:19:05,562
My name,

255
00:19:06,797 --> 00:19:07,798
my birth,

256
00:19:09,805 --> 00:19:10,806
my family,

257
00:19:13,546 --> 00:19:16,682
everything I am, is everything you're trying to tear down.

258
00:19:21,338 --> 00:19:22,762
But you're not my enemy.

259
00:19:24,293 --> 00:19:25,602
I don't think the others would see it that way.

260
00:19:27,168 --> 00:19:29,202
The Khana Ratsadon is keeping a close eye on the royal family right now.

261
00:19:30,453 --> 00:19:32,362
My father is on the opposite side from you as well.

262
00:19:34,514 --> 00:19:36,082
If you continue to be around with me,

263
00:19:37,337 --> 00:19:38,962
they will suspect you too.

264
00:19:40,274 --> 00:19:43,325
I don't want to be the reason you have to choose

265
00:19:45,253 --> 00:19:46,254
between me

266
00:19:47,254 --> 00:19:48,522
and everything you believe in.

267
00:20:11,874 --> 00:20:12,875
Phob, thank you

268
00:20:16,602 --> 00:20:17,603
for everything.

269
00:21:11,187 --> 00:21:13,082
I'll be looking forward to seeing you succeed.

270
00:22:00,013 --> 00:22:03,402
Even if we sold everything of value in the palace,

271
00:22:04,128 --> 00:22:05,842
it still wouldn't bring in 100,000 baht.

272
00:22:09,552 --> 00:22:11,362
Economy is in bad shapre right now.

273
00:22:13,573 --> 00:22:15,522
I doubt any of it will be easy to sell.

274
00:22:20,949 --> 00:22:22,442
They gave us only two weeks.

275
00:22:24,016 --> 00:22:25,522
They're deliberately trying to back us into a corner.

276
00:22:26,088 --> 00:22:27,902
There's no way we can find that money in such a short time.

277
00:22:44,012 --> 00:22:45,013
Actually,

278
00:22:46,117 --> 00:22:47,594
I went to see an English friend of mine.

279
00:22:50,485 --> 00:22:52,252
They are looking for a place to turn into a hotel.

280
00:22:56,010 --> 00:22:57,402
He told me

281
00:22:59,422 --> 00:23:00,802
he'd be willing to buy our palace

282
00:23:02,728 --> 00:23:04,122
for 100,000 baht.

283
00:23:22,781 --> 00:23:24,042
Is selling this palace

284
00:23:27,352 --> 00:23:29,162
really our only option?

285
00:23:48,426 --> 00:23:49,842
Take the money

286
00:23:50,842 --> 00:23:53,282
and make a good life for yourself.

287
00:23:54,650 --> 00:23:56,802
Make an honest living,

288
00:23:57,869 --> 00:23:59,162
and take good care of yourself.

289
00:24:00,637 --> 00:24:02,562
I'm sorry

290
00:24:04,450 --> 00:24:08,922
I couldn't take care of all of you until the very end.

291
00:24:21,744 --> 00:24:25,082
Thank you for everything you've done over the years,

292
00:24:25,621 --> 00:24:28,402
for taking care of this palace and of our family.

293
00:24:32,872 --> 00:24:33,873
Aum,

294
00:24:35,082 --> 00:24:36,083
this is yours.

295
00:24:40,106 --> 00:24:41,882
I am not going anywhere.

296
00:24:44,370 --> 00:24:49,042
You've cared for me and raised me since I was a little girl.

297
00:24:51,272 --> 00:24:54,202
Please let me go with you and take care of you, Your Highness.

298
00:24:57,458 --> 00:24:58,642
Oh, Aum.

299
00:25:00,130 --> 00:25:01,382
I don't even know

300
00:25:02,984 --> 00:25:04,845
what our lives will be like

301
00:25:05,533 --> 00:25:07,722
from now on.

302
00:25:09,725 --> 00:25:11,768
Don't stay and suffer alongside us.

303
00:25:11,997 --> 00:25:13,452
I'm not scared of hardship.

304
00:25:14,162 --> 00:25:15,394
I'm not scared at all.

305
00:25:16,354 --> 00:25:19,722
Please let me go with you and take care of you.

306
00:25:31,096 --> 00:25:33,302
Thank you.

307
00:26:25,890 --> 00:26:26,891
Vasin, dear.

308
00:26:45,533 --> 00:26:46,534
It's okay.

309
00:26:47,554 --> 00:26:49,122
It's going to be okay.

310
00:26:52,269 --> 00:26:53,722
We will stay together.

311
00:26:54,985 --> 00:26:56,522
We will get through this together.

312
00:26:58,239 --> 00:27:00,122
I love you, dear.

313
00:27:00,829 --> 00:27:02,362
I love you.

314
00:27:40,648 --> 00:27:44,402
I hereby appoint you as my knight.

315
00:27:45,642 --> 00:27:46,643
Thank you, Your Highness.

316
00:27:53,376 --> 00:27:56,402
May I offer you this cotton rose, Your Highness?

317
00:27:56,928 --> 00:27:58,502
- No!
- Why not?

318
00:27:58,933 --> 00:27:59,934
I have a better idea.

319
00:28:01,610 --> 00:28:02,611
This is better.

320
00:28:03,157 --> 00:28:04,502
Oh, come on.

321
00:28:06,490 --> 00:28:07,602
Aww, so cute.

322
00:28:09,801 --> 00:28:10,802
I can't take it off?

323
00:28:10,864 --> 00:28:12,322
You can't. You have to wear it like this.

324
00:28:13,178 --> 00:28:14,562
It looks better this way.

325
00:29:11,162 --> 00:29:13,082
[Varakulvatin Palace]

326
00:29:18,768 --> 00:29:20,082
They sold Varakulvatin Palace?

327
00:29:20,752 --> 00:29:22,353
I just found out about it.

328
00:29:22,528 --> 00:29:24,529
Some foreigners bought it and will turn it into a hotel.

329
00:29:25,362 --> 00:29:27,302
When are they moving out? And where are they going to live?

330
00:29:28,240 --> 00:29:29,802
We don't know about that.

331
00:30:21,202 --> 00:30:22,203
Your Highness?

332
00:30:23,722 --> 00:30:24,802
Where are you now?

333
00:30:27,042 --> 00:30:28,282
But I wil find you

334
00:30:29,501 --> 00:30:30,962
no matter what.

335
00:31:38,253 --> 00:31:40,202
Do we really have to live here?

336
00:31:42,664 --> 00:31:43,665
And whose fault is it that

337
00:31:44,157 --> 00:31:46,802
we have no roof over our heads and had to come all the way here?

338
00:31:46,902 --> 00:31:47,903
It's because of Phob.

339
00:31:49,010 --> 00:31:50,282
He betrayed the nation

340
00:31:50,578 --> 00:31:52,442
and seized power. That's why we've fallen this far.

341
00:32:31,949 --> 00:32:32,950
Phob.

342
00:32:34,261 --> 00:32:36,682
What people from Varakulvatin family need to face

343
00:32:37,173 --> 00:32:38,562
is not your fault at all.

344
00:32:39,040 --> 00:32:40,773
You did everything in your power to help them,

345
00:32:41,024 --> 00:32:42,714
despite drawing the attention of your superiors.

346
00:32:45,530 --> 00:32:46,562
I once believed that

347
00:32:49,242 --> 00:32:50,757
if the world changed,

348
00:32:52,037 --> 00:32:53,362
it would become easier for us

349
00:32:54,672 --> 00:32:56,642
to love each other.

350
00:32:58,103 --> 00:32:59,282
But instead,

351
00:33:00,957 --> 00:33:04,562
it's only pushed us further apart.

352
00:33:19,325 --> 00:33:20,642
Don't get ahead of yourself, okay?

353
00:33:21,848 --> 00:33:22,849
Just stay calm,

354
00:33:23,602 --> 00:33:26,403
and we'll figure out where Prince Tinnakorn has gone.

355
00:33:36,064 --> 00:33:37,602
Alright, let's eat.

356
00:33:38,682 --> 00:33:41,122
We'll eat what we have.

357
00:33:41,458 --> 00:33:43,976
At least we still have something to eat.

358
00:33:45,298 --> 00:33:46,299
Grandma?

359
00:33:46,402 --> 00:33:47,482
Aum, water please.

360
00:33:48,253 --> 00:33:49,562
Should you go to see a doctor?

361
00:33:50,042 --> 00:33:52,162
It's okay. I'm okay.

362
00:33:52,602 --> 00:33:54,762
It's probably from all the dust.

363
00:33:54,842 --> 00:33:56,843
I'll get better when I have some water.

364
00:34:04,776 --> 00:34:05,777
Are you feeling better?

365
00:34:06,952 --> 00:34:07,953
I'm fine.

366
00:34:09,589 --> 00:34:10,962
I'm going to Korat tomorrow.

367
00:34:12,402 --> 00:34:13,403
Why do you have to go?

368
00:34:15,472 --> 00:34:18,002
I've been asked to meet with some members of the royal family.

369
00:34:19,602 --> 00:34:22,882
There are still many who stand against all of this.

370
00:34:24,352 --> 00:34:26,042
Maybe there's still a chance.

371
00:34:28,160 --> 00:34:29,161
Dad,

372
00:34:30,741 --> 00:34:33,162
I don't think you should be involved with this anymore.

373
00:34:34,949 --> 00:34:37,002
We have no money, no power,

374
00:34:37,050 --> 00:34:39,552
nothing left to fight them with. Please don't get involved.

375
00:34:40,674 --> 00:34:42,136
I'm worried about you.

376
00:34:42,189 --> 00:34:43,190
I'm not scared.

377
00:34:45,720 --> 00:34:47,922
I refuse to let us live in such disgrace.

378
00:34:49,440 --> 00:34:51,002
I will restore the honor

379
00:34:51,733 --> 00:34:53,802
and dignity of our family.

380
00:34:56,746 --> 00:34:58,602
If our house is to fall while I'm the one responsible for it,

381
00:34:59,343 --> 00:35:01,602
how could I ever face our ancestors?

382
00:35:06,736 --> 00:35:07,737
You need to pack your bag.

383
00:35:08,357 --> 00:35:09,358
You are coming with me.

384
00:35:10,482 --> 00:35:11,762
Do I have to come with you?

385
00:35:12,445 --> 00:35:15,482
I can't let you out of my sight, or you'll get in trouble again.

386
00:35:23,162 --> 00:35:24,322
Let's eat.

387
00:35:26,237 --> 00:35:27,802
I want to have Gaeng Ran Juan.

388
00:35:30,575 --> 00:35:31,802
Why don't you try this soup instead?

389
00:35:32,303 --> 00:35:34,442
It's mixed veggies soup.

390
00:35:34,452 --> 00:35:36,242
Aum made it, it's tasty.

391
00:35:39,544 --> 00:35:41,162
We don't have any vacancies.

392
00:35:42,376 --> 00:35:45,842
All we have is manual labor, do you want it?

393
00:35:46,530 --> 00:35:47,531
I'll take it.

394
00:35:47,896 --> 00:35:50,685
I'll take any job. I just need work.

395
00:35:52,306 --> 00:35:54,866
I don't think you can do it.

396
00:36:19,736 --> 00:36:21,352
Do you know how to dye fabric, Your Highness?

397
00:36:40,384 --> 00:36:43,013
All we've got here is heavy manual work.

398
00:36:44,242 --> 00:36:45,362
Do you think you can do it?

399
00:36:51,261 --> 00:36:52,262
Yes, yes.

400
00:36:53,208 --> 00:36:54,209
I can do it.

401
00:41:13,117 --> 00:41:14,118
Oh my!

402
00:41:15,202 --> 00:41:16,203
Grandma?

403
00:41:17,922 --> 00:41:18,923
Grandma!

404
00:41:20,741 --> 00:41:21,742
What's wrong?

405
00:41:22,202 --> 00:41:23,602
It's Aum.

406
00:41:23,682 --> 00:41:26,322
I asked her to watch my coconut milk in the pan,

407
00:41:26,477 --> 00:41:29,002
and she burned it every time.

408
00:41:29,069 --> 00:41:30,482
She's old and I'm sick of her already.

409
00:41:31,994 --> 00:41:33,922
Wait, what are you doing?

410
00:41:35,162 --> 00:41:37,642
We're making desserts.

411
00:41:40,973 --> 00:41:42,362
Is it because of me?

412
00:41:44,925 --> 00:41:46,402
I still couldn't find the job.

413
00:41:47,309 --> 00:41:49,802
And everybody has to be in this hardship together.

414
00:41:52,310 --> 00:41:53,602
- We have to--
- Don't say that.

415
00:41:53,717 --> 00:41:56,562
Don't blame yourself, dear.

416
00:41:56,725 --> 00:41:59,602
Let me tell you something, dear.

417
00:41:59,626 --> 00:42:02,802
In life, none of us can stay in the same place forever.

418
00:42:03,056 --> 00:42:04,362
One day you may be on top of the world,

419
00:42:04,773 --> 00:42:07,362
and the next you may fall.

420
00:42:07,616 --> 00:42:09,522
You may be crying one day

421
00:42:09,666 --> 00:42:12,042
and laughing the next.

422
00:42:12,557 --> 00:42:15,562
None of it matters.

423
00:42:15,725 --> 00:42:20,562
What truly matters is what inside here,

424
00:42:20,791 --> 00:42:23,762
whether your heart can still pick itself up and keep fighting.

425
00:42:23,858 --> 00:42:28,082
As long as we still have the strength to carry on

426
00:42:28,290 --> 00:42:30,042
and the breath in our lungs,

427
00:42:30,213 --> 00:42:34,252
we're already more fortunate than so many others, my dear.

428
00:42:35,482 --> 00:42:38,282
But you've never had to suffer like this, Grandma.

429
00:42:39,152 --> 00:42:41,082
I don't see anything wrong with that.

430
00:42:41,525 --> 00:42:44,722
It was nice having what we had before,

431
00:42:44,888 --> 00:42:49,242
but there's something good about living like this, too.

432
00:42:49,509 --> 00:42:53,762
Now we get to understand how people

433
00:42:54,021 --> 00:42:56,162
who struggle every day actually live.

434
00:42:56,400 --> 00:42:58,562
I'm okay, I don't see it as a problem.

435
00:42:59,061 --> 00:43:00,242
I can live like this.

436
00:43:02,909 --> 00:43:05,482
I think…

437
00:43:05,634 --> 00:43:08,039
maybe this isn't a punishment at all.

438
00:43:08,216 --> 00:43:11,682
Maybe it's a test or a lesson,

439
00:43:11,794 --> 00:43:15,002
and it meant to help you

440
00:43:15,038 --> 00:43:17,421
understand the world a little better.

441
00:43:21,042 --> 00:43:22,543
I never looked at it that way before, Grandma.

442
00:43:23,013 --> 00:43:24,805
Well, then start thinking that way now.

443
00:43:24,842 --> 00:43:28,373
You need to come here and give me a hand.

444
00:43:32,597 --> 00:43:34,482
Come on, let's try.

445
00:43:35,824 --> 00:43:37,797
- Follow me.
- I'll follow you.

446
00:43:37,824 --> 00:43:39,762
You have to grate the coconut like this.

447
00:43:39,917 --> 00:43:42,522
I'm so fed up with Aum. She's no help at all.

448
00:43:42,685 --> 00:43:45,842
She's acting like she's an old woman, she's forgetful.

449
00:43:46,034 --> 00:43:47,035
I'm fed up with her.

450
00:43:49,102 --> 00:43:50,922
If you called me old,

451
00:43:51,157 --> 00:43:52,662
then what about you, Your Highness?

452
00:43:52,682 --> 00:43:54,608
Are you messing with me?

453
00:43:54,613 --> 00:43:58,562
- I'll get you.
- You're still young, Your Highness.

454
00:43:58,720 --> 00:44:02,602
She burned my coconut, see? I will get her.

455
00:44:02,781 --> 00:44:04,882
- You should try.
- Can you teach me?

456
00:44:04,952 --> 00:44:08,482
Hold it with your hands like this, use both hands.

457
00:44:08,760 --> 00:44:12,002
And you push coconut gentle like this, don't push it too hard.

458
00:44:12,102 --> 00:44:13,103
That's right.

459
00:44:16,648 --> 00:44:18,362
Pongpang!

460
00:44:38,120 --> 00:44:39,402
Wishing you lots of sales, Aum.

461
00:44:39,442 --> 00:44:41,082
- Thank you.
- Please take care of my grandma.

462
00:44:41,122 --> 00:44:42,123
Sure, don't worry.

463
00:44:43,296 --> 00:44:44,297
Grandma,

464
00:44:44,824 --> 00:44:47,162
a school called me in for a job interview today.

465
00:44:48,114 --> 00:44:51,802
That's great. See, I told you.

466
00:44:51,882 --> 00:44:53,842
If you don't give up,

467
00:44:53,883 --> 00:44:56,402
you will always figure something out.

468
00:44:57,242 --> 00:44:59,082
May I have your blessing, Grandma?

469
00:44:59,242 --> 00:45:00,362
Of course, you can.

470
00:45:02,642 --> 00:45:06,643
May everything go your way today,

471
00:45:06,754 --> 00:45:09,522
and may you get the job your heart desires, my dear.

472
00:45:11,632 --> 00:45:13,722
Thank you so much, Grandma.

473
00:45:22,962 --> 00:45:25,362
- I should go.
- Good luck, dear.

474
00:45:25,663 --> 00:45:26,664
Thank you.

475
00:45:30,802 --> 00:45:33,103
[Will the people gain freedom, or merely trade one master for another?]

476
00:45:34,136 --> 00:45:35,502
Pongpang!

477
00:45:42,450 --> 00:45:44,082
They just keep twisting the truth.

478
00:45:46,982 --> 00:45:49,422
The people haven't seen any real results yet, so they're still afraid.

479
00:45:50,162 --> 00:45:51,962
But they're turning the people against us.

480
00:46:02,202 --> 00:46:04,203
[Wat Khlongta School]

481
00:46:07,792 --> 00:46:10,762
I never imagined we'd have someone like you teaching at our school.

482
00:46:11,117 --> 00:46:12,322
It will be a lot of work

483
00:46:12,541 --> 00:46:14,122
because you have to teach every subject,

484
00:46:14,520 --> 00:46:16,322
especially with kids of different ages all in the same class.

485
00:46:16,882 --> 00:46:18,722
Are you sure you can handle this, Your Highness?

486
00:46:19,202 --> 00:46:21,002
You can call me Tinnakorn.

487
00:46:22,362 --> 00:46:23,363
As for the work,

488
00:46:23,621 --> 00:46:25,936
no matter how demanding or exhausting it gets, I can handle it.

489
00:46:26,960 --> 00:46:29,362
Thank you so much for giving me this job.

490
00:46:38,960 --> 00:46:42,061
If you can't read or write yet,

491
00:46:42,102 --> 00:46:43,469
or if this is your first day here,

492
00:46:43,858 --> 00:46:44,859
there's no need to be shy.

493
00:46:44,978 --> 00:46:46,962
It's my first day teaching here, too.

494
00:46:49,133 --> 00:46:51,346
Today, I'm going to teach you

495
00:46:51,474 --> 00:46:53,642
how to read Thai consonants.

496
00:46:54,802 --> 00:46:57,552
These are Thai consonants.

497
00:46:57,733 --> 00:46:59,362
This is how you write the first letter.

498
00:46:59,568 --> 00:47:02,962
And it is called 'Kor.Khai', repeat after me.

499
00:47:03,442 --> 00:47:05,088
Kor.Khai.'

500
00:47:05,302 --> 00:47:06,303
Good job.

501
00:47:06,741 --> 00:47:08,242
Let's continue.

502
00:47:45,202 --> 00:47:47,902
Today, we're going to learn some math.

503
00:47:48,008 --> 00:47:50,842
Hold up your finger like me and say the number. One.

504
00:47:51,117 --> 00:47:53,282
- One.
- Plus.

505
00:47:53,512 --> 00:47:55,576
- Plus.
- The same number.

506
00:47:55,602 --> 00:47:57,642
- One.
- One.

507
00:47:57,703 --> 00:47:59,842
- Equals…
- Two.

508
00:47:59,902 --> 00:48:01,362
That's right. It means that…

509
00:48:01,448 --> 00:48:03,482
one plus one equals two.

510
00:48:06,381 --> 00:48:07,382
H.

511
00:48:07,987 --> 00:48:08,988
K.

512
00:48:10,146 --> 00:48:12,370
A-Ant.

513
00:48:12,637 --> 00:48:13,638
Meaning?

514
00:48:14,038 --> 00:48:15,039
Ant.

515
00:48:15,047 --> 00:48:16,048
Well done.

516
00:48:21,282 --> 00:48:22,882
[Nakhon Ratchasima]

517
00:48:28,885 --> 00:48:29,886
He's here, Your Highness.

518
00:48:30,602 --> 00:48:33,522
The moment I heard you were joining us, I rushed over.

519
00:48:34,296 --> 00:48:35,642
There are more people, Adul.

520
00:48:36,632 --> 00:48:38,602
There are still plenty of people who oppose them.

521
00:48:39,116 --> 00:48:40,117
Those traitors

522
00:48:40,368 --> 00:48:42,162
who want to turn Siam communist

523
00:48:42,269 --> 00:48:43,570
will all meet the same fate.

524
00:48:49,045 --> 00:48:50,642
If we get rid of those rebels,

525
00:48:51,210 --> 00:48:54,042
we'll be able to go back to the palace and live comfortably again, won't we?

526
00:49:25,602 --> 00:49:27,282
Everything is going well?

527
00:49:27,346 --> 00:49:28,808
Absolutely, sir.

528
00:49:28,941 --> 00:49:29,942
Good.

529
00:49:38,730 --> 00:49:39,731
Oh!

530
00:49:40,026 --> 00:49:41,802
Good evening, Your Highness.

531
00:49:42,133 --> 00:49:43,602
Happy birthday to you, Mr. Kitti.

532
00:49:46,992 --> 00:49:49,442
The future of Siam is in your hands now.

533
00:49:52,032 --> 00:49:53,202
Thank you, Your Highness.

534
00:49:54,010 --> 00:49:55,882
I've read the government's new laws.

535
00:49:56,437 --> 00:49:57,962
If there's anything I can do to help,

536
00:49:58,748 --> 00:50:02,042
I'd be honored to play my part in moving our country forward.

537
00:50:03,659 --> 00:50:04,660
Of course, I'll let you know.

538
00:50:05,645 --> 00:50:07,452
We can talk about that later.

539
00:50:09,037 --> 00:50:10,082
Please enjoy the party.

540
00:50:27,056 --> 00:50:28,682
Thank you, thank you so much.

541
00:50:31,253 --> 00:50:34,202
What about the project that we talked about?

542
00:50:35,802 --> 00:50:38,858
It's borning, right? I know.

543
00:50:42,952 --> 00:50:45,002
When we were planning the change of government,

544
00:50:48,344 --> 00:50:50,442
I imagined a very different Siam from the one we have now.

545
00:50:57,272 --> 00:50:58,722
The country has only just begun to change.

546
00:50:59,416 --> 00:51:02,242
You can't expect everything to be perfect overnight.

547
00:51:02,664 --> 00:51:04,402
I'm not expecting perfection.

548
00:51:06,231 --> 00:51:09,642
I just never imagined I'd live to see something like this.

549
00:51:12,821 --> 00:51:13,962
Are we turning into

550
00:51:16,042 --> 00:51:17,722
the very thing we fought against?

551
00:51:21,810 --> 00:51:23,322
Is everything okay?

552
00:51:28,850 --> 00:51:30,882
Are we really doing this for the people?

553
00:51:32,210 --> 00:51:33,242
What a weird question?

554
00:51:37,170 --> 00:51:40,562
People are unemployed out there. They're angry with us.

555
00:51:41,293 --> 00:51:42,294
And here we are,

556
00:51:43,146 --> 00:51:45,302
holding a celebration as if nothing is happening.

557
00:51:47,514 --> 00:51:49,242
People are saying we've simply replaced the old masters with new ones.

558
00:51:50,202 --> 00:51:52,802
Politics isn't driven by ideals alone.

559
00:51:53,410 --> 00:51:54,842
But when you brought us into this,

560
00:51:55,570 --> 00:51:56,882
you spoke of ideals.

561
00:51:57,122 --> 00:51:58,936
You spoke of dignity. You spoke of equality.

562
00:51:59,965 --> 00:52:02,269
Now it feels like we've forgotten why we're here.

563
00:52:02,402 --> 00:52:03,403
I've never forgotten.

564
00:52:05,378 --> 00:52:07,882
You can't govern a country with beautiful ideals written on a piece of paper.

565
00:52:08,253 --> 00:52:10,682
We have to make compromises, forge alliances,

566
00:52:10,866 --> 00:52:12,496
and bring those with power to our side.

567
00:52:12,992 --> 00:52:16,122
Otherwise, the government won't survive, and the country won't move forward.

568
00:52:18,058 --> 00:52:19,522
And what about the people who believed in us?

569
00:52:21,194 --> 00:52:22,762
The people who put their hopes in us?

570
00:52:23,765 --> 00:52:25,242
How many more years do you expect them to wait?

571
00:52:26,448 --> 00:52:28,242
Do you really think you can change a country

572
00:52:29,306 --> 00:52:30,502
without getting your hands dirty?

573
00:52:31,887 --> 00:52:32,888
If you do,

574
00:52:35,159 --> 00:52:37,002
you're far too naive.

575
00:52:44,354 --> 00:52:45,355
This way, sir.

576
00:52:46,738 --> 00:52:47,882
Happy birthday, sir.

577
00:52:48,024 --> 00:52:51,002
Thank you, thank you so much.

578
00:52:51,282 --> 00:52:52,283
Thank you.

579
00:52:54,351 --> 00:52:55,352
Thank you everyone.

580
00:54:34,096 --> 00:54:36,482
Hello, Mr. Tin.

581
00:54:36,832 --> 00:54:38,858
Whoa! There are a lot of fruits.

582
00:54:39,088 --> 00:54:42,402
The students gave me a lot of fruit, so I thought I'd share some with you.

583
00:54:42,672 --> 00:54:44,282
These rambutans are from Sompol.

584
00:54:44,698 --> 00:54:46,642
Mangosteens are from Niyom's orchard.

585
00:54:46,800 --> 00:54:48,962
And I think Santols are from Noknoi.

586
00:54:49,568 --> 00:54:51,042
You remember them all?

587
00:54:51,413 --> 00:54:54,242
I used to buy fruit and vegetables from their parents all the time.

588
00:54:55,034 --> 00:54:56,432
Then they started sending their kids to school.

589
00:54:56,784 --> 00:54:59,322
I've gone from being their customer to their teacher.

590
00:55:01,338 --> 00:55:02,339
Right.

591
00:55:03,602 --> 00:55:04,603
Yeah?

592
00:55:04,656 --> 00:55:06,302
The ministry wanted us to explain

593
00:55:06,322 --> 00:55:08,002
the new government system to the students.

594
00:55:11,842 --> 00:55:14,202
[The People's Party Proclamation of 1932, No. 1]

595
00:55:20,325 --> 00:55:21,802
It used to be quiet around here,

596
00:55:22,981 --> 00:55:25,082
but these days, more and more kids are coming to school.

597
00:55:25,818 --> 00:55:27,482
Their parents sent their kids to school,

598
00:55:27,741 --> 00:55:29,602
they want them to learn to read and write,

599
00:55:29,622 --> 00:55:31,202
so they can have an easier life than their parents.

600
00:55:32,802 --> 00:55:35,922
It's a good thing the government is putting money into education.

601
00:55:37,408 --> 00:55:39,722
I don't know where all this politics is going,

602
00:55:40,485 --> 00:55:41,562
but as long as

603
00:55:41,717 --> 00:55:45,082
the kids are getting an education, I suppose things can't be all that bad.

604
00:56:04,258 --> 00:56:07,120
Mr. Tin, can you check this for me? Did I get it right?

605
00:56:07,152 --> 00:56:08,153
Let me see.

606
00:56:08,960 --> 00:56:12,842
"When I grow up, I want to be like my teacher, Mr. Tin."

607
00:56:14,442 --> 00:56:17,682
"So I don't have to work in the fields or on a farm."

608
00:56:18,637 --> 00:56:20,682
"I can have money to take care of my grandma,"

609
00:56:21,058 --> 00:56:23,122
"and my mom, who's sick at him."

610
00:56:24,056 --> 00:56:25,452
"I want to be a good person."

611
00:56:28,896 --> 00:56:30,032
Excellent! You got them all right.

612
00:56:30,314 --> 00:56:31,315
Thank you.

613
00:56:32,336 --> 00:56:34,337
- You can continue writing.
- Okay.

614
00:56:34,586 --> 00:56:36,002
I'll do my very best.

615
00:56:36,480 --> 00:56:37,481
Keep it up.

616
00:56:55,501 --> 00:56:57,922
- Phob.
- Hello, Janthorn.

617
00:57:00,725 --> 00:57:04,482
Auntie, can I trouble you for another meal today?

618
00:57:04,688 --> 00:57:05,689
Sure, you can.

619
00:57:06,544 --> 00:57:08,543
What do you have here?

620
00:57:09,957 --> 00:57:12,802
Someone at the printing house brought this for me. They said it's really good.

621
00:57:15,461 --> 00:57:17,922
It looks so good.

622
00:57:26,533 --> 00:57:27,802
This dessert

623
00:57:29,534 --> 00:57:31,202
reminded me of the one that Princess made.

624
00:57:33,538 --> 00:57:36,322
I used to help her back then.

625
00:57:38,922 --> 00:57:41,322
I have no idea

626
00:57:42,277 --> 00:57:43,842
how they are doing right now.

627
00:57:52,954 --> 00:57:55,602
Can I help you in the kitchen today?

628
00:57:55,861 --> 00:57:57,602
Maybe some of your cooking magic will rub off on me.

629
00:57:58,229 --> 00:57:59,230
Let's go.

630
00:58:33,885 --> 00:58:34,886
I'm here.

631
00:58:40,986 --> 00:58:41,987
Wow!

632
00:58:43,173 --> 00:58:44,174
Thank you, Your Highness.

633
00:58:44,826 --> 00:58:46,562
I helped Grandma make some desserts.

634
00:58:53,904 --> 00:58:54,905
I…

635
00:58:56,933 --> 00:58:58,242
Let me guess.

636
00:58:59,605 --> 00:59:00,606
This is the one

637
00:59:02,045 --> 00:59:03,282
that you made, isn't it?

638
00:59:05,005 --> 00:59:06,006
How did you know?

639
00:59:06,146 --> 00:59:09,162
It's bigger than the rest.

640
00:59:09,490 --> 00:59:10,491
And the color is too bright.

641
00:59:11,085 --> 00:59:12,842
I don't think your grandma made this one.

642
00:59:14,733 --> 00:59:15,882
You don't have to eat them.

643
00:59:16,045 --> 00:59:17,826
Oh, come on.

644
00:59:18,221 --> 00:59:19,602
I am starving.

645
00:59:20,168 --> 00:59:24,042
They're huge, misshapen, and look ridiculous.

646
00:59:24,248 --> 00:59:26,082
You'll only end up with an upset stomach. Don't eat them.

647
00:59:26,978 --> 00:59:29,642
Oh, Your Highness. Come on.

648
00:59:30,039 --> 00:59:31,040
I was just joking.

649
00:59:34,605 --> 00:59:35,606
Well.

650
00:59:37,288 --> 00:59:40,202
They may look a little strange,

651
00:59:41,128 --> 00:59:42,322
but I think they'll be the most delicious of all.

652
00:59:44,722 --> 00:59:47,302
Stop trying, it won't work.

653
00:59:55,138 --> 00:59:56,722
- Is it good?
- It's good.

654
00:59:58,413 --> 00:59:59,414
This is the best.

655
01:00:00,406 --> 01:00:01,562
Then you should sit properly to eat it.

656
01:00:07,333 --> 01:00:08,362
This is so good.

657
01:00:08,426 --> 01:00:10,082
- Let me try.
- I'll feed you.

658
01:00:17,797 --> 01:00:18,798
What do you think?

659
01:00:19,573 --> 01:00:20,574
It is good.

660
01:00:21,040 --> 01:00:22,041
Because?

661
01:00:22,490 --> 01:00:23,962
Because this isn't the one I made.

662
01:00:32,802 --> 01:00:34,202
[Constitutional Government Knowledge Contest]

663
01:00:34,212 --> 01:00:35,813
[Organized by Ministry of Public Instruction — December 8, 1932]

664
01:00:40,013 --> 01:00:41,242
Their school is so nice.

665
01:00:42,509 --> 01:00:43,510
Don't be cared.

666
01:00:44,360 --> 01:00:46,682
Believe in yourself. You can do it.

667
01:00:47,336 --> 01:00:49,362
I'm so nervous I feel like I'm going to pee myself, sir.

668
01:00:50,258 --> 01:00:52,042
We should get going.

669
01:00:52,422 --> 01:00:54,690
At this rate, you'll end up answering questions and
peeing your pants at the same time.

670
01:00:54,994 --> 01:00:57,133
If you'll excuse us, we'd better go to the bathroom.

671
01:00:57,234 --> 01:00:59,162
Of course. Go ahead and use the bathroom first.

672
01:00:59,805 --> 01:01:01,002
Let's go.

673
01:01:38,296 --> 01:01:39,297
Your Highness,

674
01:01:44,272 --> 01:01:45,402
what are you doing here?

675
01:01:49,322 --> 01:01:51,302
I'm here with my students for a quiz competition.

676
01:01:53,024 --> 01:01:54,025
Your students?

677
01:01:56,762 --> 01:01:57,763
Right,

678
01:01:58,314 --> 01:02:00,762
I am a teacher...Mr. Tin.

679
01:02:04,024 --> 01:02:05,025
What about you?

680
01:02:09,208 --> 01:02:10,602
I'm representing my department

681
01:02:11,810 --> 01:02:14,002
on the judging panel, Your Highness.

682
01:02:25,658 --> 01:02:27,282
I hope you're doing well.

683
01:02:29,658 --> 01:02:30,659
I am doing well, thanks.

684
01:02:33,402 --> 01:02:34,403
And you?

685
01:02:39,546 --> 01:02:40,547
I…

686
01:02:42,538 --> 01:02:43,539
I'm fine, I guess.

687
01:02:49,506 --> 01:02:50,642
You don't seem to be doing too well yourself.

688
01:02:52,265 --> 01:02:53,266
Is everything okay?

689
01:03:01,653 --> 01:03:02,762
We're being criticized

690
01:03:03,605 --> 01:03:05,642
for acting too hastily and

691
01:03:07,010 --> 01:03:08,011
being too impatient,

692
01:03:08,981 --> 01:03:10,882
for pushing through change before the country was ready for it.

693
01:03:13,509 --> 01:03:14,762
At first,

694
01:03:16,130 --> 01:03:17,242
I thought that

695
01:03:18,312 --> 01:03:19,562
after we'd changed the system,

696
01:03:20,904 --> 01:03:22,452
many things would improve.

697
01:03:24,109 --> 01:03:25,110
But even now,

698
01:03:26,288 --> 01:03:27,389
people are still struggling.

699
01:03:29,216 --> 01:03:30,322
There are still those competing for power

700
01:03:33,258 --> 01:03:34,562
and those taking advantage of the situation, just as before.

701
01:03:40,202 --> 01:03:41,203
Sometimes

702
01:03:42,658 --> 01:03:43,922
I can't help but wonder...

703
01:03:47,554 --> 01:03:49,302
was everything I lost

704
01:03:52,429 --> 01:03:53,842
really worth it?

705
01:03:59,234 --> 01:04:00,902
It doesn't matter anymore

706
01:04:03,117 --> 01:04:04,502
whether it happened too soon or too late.

707
01:04:07,768 --> 01:04:09,482
The change has already happened.

708
01:04:12,370 --> 01:04:15,562
What matters now is what we do to make things better.

709
01:04:22,733 --> 01:04:23,734
You're right.

710
01:04:25,362 --> 01:04:26,822
I'm still trying to figure out

711
01:04:27,898 --> 01:04:29,202
what I should do.

712
01:04:31,765 --> 01:04:32,922
I still have my doubts.

713
01:04:34,102 --> 01:04:35,103
Phob.

714
01:04:37,602 --> 01:04:39,362
We can't always have things go our way.

715
01:04:40,893 --> 01:04:41,894
Look at me.

716
01:04:43,533 --> 01:04:46,642
I used to think my life

717
01:04:47,182 --> 01:04:48,283
had already been mapped out for me.

718
01:04:51,010 --> 01:04:52,242
And yet, here I am, having to start all over again.

719
01:04:55,762 --> 01:04:56,763
And you know what?

720
01:04:58,573 --> 01:04:59,842
Some of the students in my class

721
01:05:02,052 --> 01:05:05,002
couldn't even write their own names at first.

722
01:05:06,602 --> 01:05:08,522
Some of them almost never got the chance to go to school.

723
01:05:10,064 --> 01:05:11,632
But now they can read

724
01:05:13,584 --> 01:05:14,722
and write.

725
01:05:17,106 --> 01:05:18,302
They dare to think for themselves.

726
01:05:20,520 --> 01:05:21,562
They dare to dream.

727
01:05:23,890 --> 01:05:25,522
Maybe what you've done

728
01:05:27,119 --> 01:05:29,120
hasn't made a difference on a larger scale yet.

729
01:05:32,202 --> 01:05:33,242
But at the very least...

730
01:05:36,636 --> 01:05:37,637
it's already beginning

731
01:05:38,626 --> 01:05:40,502
to make a difference in someone's life.

732
01:05:48,373 --> 01:05:49,452
I am rooting for you.

733
01:05:51,514 --> 01:05:52,515
Don't give up on your dream.

734
01:05:59,520 --> 01:06:01,051
You look so strong.

735
01:06:02,613 --> 01:06:04,522
I'm just trying to keep moving forward.

736
01:06:07,296 --> 01:06:08,297
You should too.

737
01:06:11,936 --> 01:06:12,937
Stay strong,

738
01:06:16,405 --> 01:06:17,406
all right?

739
01:06:35,088 --> 01:06:37,541
I need to get going.

740
01:06:39,317 --> 01:06:40,318
I wish you the best of luck.

741
01:06:41,504 --> 01:06:42,505
I'll see you later.

742
01:06:44,522 --> 01:06:45,523
See you later, Your Highness.

743
01:07:44,883 --> 01:07:46,115
If I ever get another chance,

744
01:07:46,536 --> 01:07:49,280
I hope he'll open his heart to me again, even just a little.

745
01:07:49,955 --> 01:07:51,840
I still want to be by his side.

746
01:07:52,939 --> 01:07:56,400
The cotton rose tree? You miss him, don't you?

747
01:07:58,267 --> 01:08:00,900
My source says there's been some unusual activity.

748
01:08:00,920 --> 01:08:02,920
It seems Prince Vasin is really going through with it this time.

749
01:08:05,800 --> 01:08:08,520
Soon, everything will be back to the way it was.

750
01:08:08,664 --> 01:08:10,040
What do you mean?

751
01:08:13,142 --> 01:08:15,000
Are you okay, Your Highness?

752
01:08:15,840 --> 01:08:16,841
Phob.

